+---------------- DISCRETE SAFETY LATCH ----------------+

  INPUT FAULT LINE:
    FIRE_FAULT_LINE --> [QSET] NPN

  LATCH:
    [QSET] and [QRESET] form a cross‑coupled pair:

      QSET collector ----+----[R1]----> base of QLATCH
                         |
      QRESET collector --+----[R2]----> base of QLATCH_BAR

      QLATCH and QLATCH_BAR are NPNs in SR‑latch topology.

  OUTPUT:
    QLATCH collector ----> LATCH_OUT (HIGH = fault latched)
    LATCH_OUT ----> DISABLE_DRIVER

  RESET:
    [RESET_SW] momentary to pull base of QRESET high
      → forces LATCH_OUT low → re‑enable driver (if no new fault)

  BEHAVIOR:
  - First FIRE_FAULT_LINE pulse sets latch → DISABLE_DRIVER stays active.
  - System will not auto‑restart even if sensors recover.
  - Manual RESET required, giving human oversight before re‑enable.
